---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout title="About">
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About DEUCE</h1>
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href={base}>Home</a> / About</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="content">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>The Project</h2>
      <p>
        The DEUCE Project is dedicated to improving the enforcement of judicial decisions in cross-border
        pecuniary claims across the European Union. It focuses on judgments, authentic instruments, and
        court settlements, with the aim of making enforcement procedures clearer, more efficient, and fully digital.
      </p>

      <h2>Addressing Enforcement Challenges</h2>
      <p>
        One of the project's core objectives is to address the lack of harmonisation among EU Member States'
        enforcement rules, which currently creates significant obstacles for the cross-border enforcement of
        European Enforcement Orders (EEO) and European Orders for Payment (EOP). This fragmentation makes it
        difficult for creditors, as well as legal professionals such as lawyers and bailiffs, to navigate and
        apply enforcement rules across different jurisdictions.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Solutions</h2>
      <p>
        To overcome these challenges, the DEUCE Project develops a comprehensive roadmap of enforcement rules
        in 26 EU Member States, alongside a user-friendly IT platform offering practical guidance on EEO and EOP
        enforcement procedures. In parallel, the project designs a blockchain-based system to support simplified,
        secure, and digital enforcement processes, with the broader goal of enhancing citizens' access to justice
        across the Union.
      </p>

      <h2>Project Consortium</h2>
      <p>
        The project brings together a multidisciplinary consortium of experts in international civil procedure,
        private law, and information technology. Through close collaboration, the consortium works to clarify
        existing enforcement frameworks, promote best practices, and deliver innovative, technology-driven solutions.
      </p>

      <h2>Stakeholder Engagement</h2>
      <p>
        The DEUCE Project actively involves a wide range of stakeholders, including creditors, lawyers, bailiffs,
        notaries, consumer associations, and policymakers. By engaging practitioners and end-users across Europe,
        the project ensures that its outcomes are practical, validated, and responsive to real-world enforcement needs.
      </p>

      <h2>EU Funding</h2>
      <p>
        This project is co-funded by the European Union's Justice Programme (2021-2027). The content of this
        website represents the views of the author only and is their sole responsibility. The European Commission
        does not accept any responsibility for use that may be made of the information it contains.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
